# AI Secretary — local environment template.
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. NEVER commit the filled-in file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every value has a working default so `npm run dev` works unmodified for a
# first try. AI credentials are configured in the web UI (Settings → AI
# Providers) — there is NO AI key in this file and no proprietary AI SDK.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite (default, simplest): a single file. Fine for dev and single-box installs.
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
#
# Postgres is the production target. Point at your own instance:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/ais?schema=public"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AES-256-GCM key material for encrypting provider API keys and integration
# credentials at rest. If unset, the app generates `.data/secret.key` on first
# boot and reuses it (fine for single-box installs as long as that file persists).
#
# Generate a strong one:   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# WARNING: changing APP_SECRET later does NOT re-encrypt stored secrets —
# existing provider keys/integration credentials become unusable and must be
# re-entered. See docs/SELF_HOSTING.md.
# APP_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Networking (Twilio / inbound webhooks only — not needed for local use)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The absolute public base URL of this deployment, used as a fallback when
# validating Twilio webhook signatures. The integration's own publicBaseUrl
# takes precedence. Not used for payment webhooks.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://receptionist.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI provider (BYOK — configured in the web UI, not here)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is intentionally NO AI credential here. After the app is running, go to
# Settings → AI Providers and pick either:
#   - a local Ollama server (http://localhost:11434) — fully offline, free
#   - any OpenAI-compatible endpoint + your own API key (OpenAI, Groq, Together,
#     Mistral, vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp server, …)
# Knowledge/RAG embeddings work out of the box with the built-in local model
# (no credentials, no network after the first model download).
